					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Gotta upvote for that image, if nothing else. Great effect.</p> <p>I do have to be honest, this was pretty dense. I was mostly confused as to whether the KTE designation was for the initial meme, the countermeme, both, or either on a sliding scale. I guess the story is they're trying to eradicate an issue like that one skip from a while ago, that destroys all ability to communicate. (Is this related? Is that even allowed?) And they develop a counter to it that&#8230; basically just does the same thing?</p> <p>Yeah, definitely confused.</p> 
				 	]]>
